OL,3,GNEWSATeacher's late night emails to
OL,4,Apupil 'not sexual'
OL,5,
OL,6,FA maths teacher who promised to find a
OL,7,Fschoolgirl the "perfect boyfriend" in a
OL,8,Flate-night email chat has been allowed
OL,9,Fto continue teaching.
OL,11,FJamil Wali, who worked at King's
OL,12,FLeadership Academy in Liverpool,
OL,13,Fexchanged more than 200 emails with the
OL,14,Fstudent, telling her in messages sent
OL,15,Fas late as 23:00  that "I am always
OL,16,Fhere", and "I got your back".
OL,18,FWali admitted to "excessive" and
OL,19,F"inappropriate" contact with the pupil
OL,20,Fbut said the emails were motivated by
OL,21,Fconcern for the "vulnerable" girl's
OL,22,Fwellbeing.
OL,23,APub: 21-AugQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageB NW Eng NewsC Reg TVF Weather
